        "description": {
            "value": "<p><em>Capricorn &mdash; 3rd (Cloth Ability) Technique, gained at level 11.</em></p><p><em>Both arms as blades &mdash; the technique that cuts twice in the space of one cut.</em></p><p>Make <strong>two unarmed Strikes</strong> against a single creature within reach. Both are made at your <strong>full attack modifier with no multiple attack penalty</strong>, both gain <strong>deadly d12</strong>, and both ignore Hardness, resistance, and immunity to physical damage.</p><p><strong>If both hit</strong>, the target must attempt a Fortitude save against your Cosmo DC; on a failure it is <strong>severed</strong>, as The Sharpest Sword.</p><p>The activity counts as two attacks for your multiple attack penalty afterward.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightening (+2 levels)</strong> Each Strike deals an additional 1d8 slashing damage.</p><p>On a day your constellation is <strong>Ascendant</strong> this Technique heightens as though you were 4 levels higher; on a <strong>Zenith</strong>, 8 levels higher.</p><hr /><p><strong>Automation note:</strong> in the guide this Technique's bonus damage starts at <em>zero</em> and is purely a heightening rider, but a pf2e spell needs a base formula to scale from. The base here is <strong>1d1</strong> &mdash; a flat 1 point, deliberately beneath notice &mdash; so that the heightening steps and the sky's bonus dice both apply automatically instead of being tracked by hand.</p>"
        },
